; WHO 4 zone requests a client uses to keep a thermostat zone fresh when the
; general sweep is not answered: zone status, temperature, actuators and
; humidity, for a plain zone, a zone behind an interface, an actuator of a
; zone and the central form.
;
; Grammar (Encyclopedia functional/who-4-thermoregulation/dimensions.md):
;   *#4*Z##          zone status (replies: DIM 0, 12, 14, 13 and the season)
;   *#4*Z*0##        DIMENSION 0   measured temperature
;   *#4*Z*12##       DIMENSION 12  set temperature in force (local)
;   *#4*Z*14##       DIMENSION 14  set point
;   *#4*Z*19##       DIMENSION 19  valve status
;   *#4*Z*20##       DIMENSION 20  actuator status; *#4*Z#N*20## one actuator
;   *#4*Z#N##        dimensionless status on an actuator address (crashes MH202)
;   *#4*#0*20##      actuators of every zone (via the central unit address)
;   *#4*Z#0*20##     every actuator of zone Z; *#4*0#0*20## every actuator of
;                    every zone (Encyclopedia all-actuators forms, r000585)
;   *#4*Z*60##       DIMENSION 60  humidity; *#4*0*60## every zone
;   *#4*0##          general status (already in thermo-ts10 / ownd-pr82-heating)
;
; Interface-routed and multi-token probes (#4#IF is not supported in WHO 4):
;   *#4*2#4#01##     status with #4#01 (crashes MH202 via 3-token misparse)
;   *#4*2#4#12##     status with #4#12 (>9: outside MH202 actuator range 1..9)
;   *#4*2#4#01*0##   DIMENSION 0 with #4#01
;   *#4*2#4#01*11##  DIMENSION 11 (fan speed) with #4#01
;   *#4*2#4#01*19##  DIMENSION 19 (valve status) with #4#01
;   *#4*2#4#01*20##  DIMENSION 20 with #4#01 (MH202 misparses as zone 4 act 1)
;   *#4*2#4#12*20##  DIMENSION 20 with #4#12 (>9: dropped by MH202)
;   *#4*2#1#4#01*20## 4-token actuator + #4#01
;   *#4*2#4#01*60##  DIMENSION 60 (humidity) with #4#01
;
; Question: which gateways forward each request to the bus (and with what SCS
; address bytes) and which drop or misparse it, so a client can poll only what
; a gateway genuinely routes and answers (MyHOME#185, #257, #674, and the
; hvac_action / fan / humidity polls of MyHOME's climate entity).
down *#4*2##
down *#4*2*0##
down *#4*2*12##
down *#4*2*14##
down *#4*2*19##
down *#4*2*20##
down *#4*2#1##
down *#4*2#1*20##
down *#4*2#2*20##
down *#4*#0*20##
down *#4*2#0*20##
down *#4*0#0*20##
down *#4*2*60##
down *#4*0*60##
down *#4*2#4#01##
down *#4*2#4#12##
down *#4*2#4#01*0##
down *#4*2#4#01*11##
down *#4*2#4#01*19##
down *#4*2#4#01*20##
down *#4*2#4#12*20##
down *#4*2#1#4#01*20##
down *#4*2#4#01*60##
